   "source": {
    "label": "th:bandit",
    "number": "Theorem 1",
    "quote": "For any $\\delta \\in (0,1)$ and parameters $0\\le\\gamma<1/2$, $0<\\beta\\le 1$, and $\\eta>0$ satisfying $2\\eta K|\\C|\\le \\gamma$, the performance of the algorithm defined above can be bounded, with probability at least $1-\\delta$, as \\[ \\frac{1}{n}\\left( \\wh{L}_n-\\min_{\\bi\\in\\cP} L_{\\bi,n}\\right) \\le K\\gamma+2\\eta K^2|\\C| +\\frac{K}{n\\beta}\\ln\\frac{|E|}{\\delta}+\\frac{\\ln N}{n\\eta} + |E |\\beta. \\]"
   },
   "confidence": "high",
   "notes": "Per-round bound multiplied by T. Paper's K (path length) -> m, |E| -> d, n -> T."
  },
